{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the MCP outputSchema addition at exact clean pushed head 284f9002139d0c5beb44c8696f414c7976bb1cc2 on request/mcp-output-schema. Parent is current main ebdca9fa; checkout clean, origin matching. Additive interoperability only, no behaviour change.\n\nWHAT IT DOES. All fourteen tool definitions now carry outputSchema {\"type\":\"object\",\"additionalProperties\":true}, attached by a loop over the definitions rather than repeated in each, so a tool added later cannot forget it.\n\nTHE RESTRAINT IS THE DESIGN AND IT IS WHAT I MOST WANT JUDGED. Declaring an outputSchema makes conformant clients validate structuredContent against it and reject what does not conform, so a wrong schema is worse than none. I named no keys, because none could be proved present on every return path: every resident-backed tool has a degraded local-fold fallback returning a differently shaped value, and submit conditionally adds degraded, warning and projected. If you think a key is genuinely universal and I have been over-cautious, say so — but the failure I was avoiding is rejecting a response that is correct today.\n\nTYPE object IS ARGUED FROM THE CODE, not assumed. Every success path in dispatch returns either a Go map or a statusview value struct — ActorStatus, WaitDelta, WorkPage, ArtifactPage, ItemInspection — and both encode as objects. The failure path carries no structuredContent at all.\n\nTHE ENVELOPE DISTINCTION WAS CHECKED ON THE WIRE. The result's keys are _meta, content, isError, live_attention, resultType, structuredContent, so isError and live_attention are siblings rather than members. Scoping to the envelope would have produced the over-strict schema this change exists to avoid.\n\nONE CONDITION OF THE GOVERNING REQUEST IS UNMET AND I AM FLAGGING IT RATHER THAN LETTING IT PASS. It asks for verification against a real client that structuredContent is now recognised. I did not achieve that. The only real client in reach runs an older binary, so exercising it would demonstrate the old behaviour, and rebuilding or restarting the running resident was outside the row. What I verified instead: a binary built from this head, driven over stdio with a scripted JSON-RPC client against the real workroom, returns fourteen tools each with an object-typed outputSchema, and tools/call whoami returns isError false with a conforming structuredContent object. That proves the schemas are on the wire and that a real response satisfies them; it does not prove any client's interface surfaces the payload, which is what hugh reported. Your call whether that gap blocks approval or belongs in a follow-up once a client can be rebuilt.\n\nMUTATION EVIDENCE. Skipping one tool in the attach loop fails TestStatelessDiscoverAndToolList by name, naming the tool that declares no object outputSchema. Restored and green.\n\nONE PROVENANCE NOTE. The artifact rests on my promise and on 87672c8a, the cmd/gitseq-mcp artifact your completion merge published at current main. That predecessor projects stale, so my artifact inherits it; I signed the dead-basis override rather than reach for a fresher-looking but wrong basis, and the head, tree and parent are all current.\n\nGATES, run by me at this exact head from a run I watched exit, exit codes captured directly rather than through a pipe. go test ./... -count=1 exit 0: 34 ok, zero failures, zero cached. npm test 132 pass 0 fail. gofmt empty; build, vet, diff-check exit 0; make ui leaves git status empty; make ui-check exit 0.\n\nDo not merge.","body":{"branch":"request/mcp-output-schema","conditions":"Independent review of exact clean pushed head 284f9002139d0c5beb44c8696f414c7976bb1cc2 on request/mcp-output-schema, whose parent is current main ebdca9fa. Citing artifact 2008eba8 at cmd/gitseq-mcp. Governing request is planner's 206708ca; my promise is 9c20ee34. Record Architecture, Security and Simplification conclusions and file the verdict with gs review resting on that artifact. Judge in particular whether the schema is genuinely no stricter than what the tools return across every variant including the degraded fallbacks, whether scoping to structuredContent rather than the envelope is correct, and whether the unmet real-client condition should block. Do not merge.","dead_basis_override":"true","head":"284f9002139d0c5beb44c8696f414c7976bb1cc2","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}